## Interpretation note
------------------
A two-dimensional position array requires memory proportional to
the number of particles, O(N).

A pairwise displacement array has shape `(N, N, 2)`, so its
memory requirement grows quadratically, O(N²).

For the same array shape, `float32` uses half the memory of
`float64`, although it provides lower numerical precision.

Large pairwise arrays can require substantial memory as N increases.
Therefore, theoretical memory estimates are used for larger particle
counts instead of allocating very large arrays.

The results demonstrate how numerical precision and array dimensions
affect memory usage and the scalability of a 2D particle simulation.
